From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mihawk <163614687+mihawk-99@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 01 Nov 2026 14:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] kernelbase: PS5: No debugger starts in a title or helper.

A crash in a PS5 title or helper started winedbg: UnhandledExceptionFilter calls the game's own filter, then start_debugger,
which reads AeDebug and allocates the command line and a copy of the environment from the process heap. The runtime has no
winedbg (the log shows "cannot open .../winedbg.so"), and when the crashing thread's neighbours hold the heap lock the crash
froze the title instead of ending it (prospero-win saw this in a game, from the heap lock; here the tester's Elden Ring crash
started a winedbg that itself failed 0.65 s later). WINE_PS5_NTDLL_DIR is set by the starter for a title and for each helper:
there the filter still calls the game's own filter, then logs the exception ("no debugger starts in a PS5 title") and lets the
thread's handler end the process.

The problem was found by reading prospero-win (mpereiraesaa/prospero-win, LGPL-2.1-or-later; its patch 0971, commit b9ee658);
this change is written independently here (NOTICE.md, "prospero-win and ProsperoMC"). Not run on a console.
---
 dlls/kernelbase/debug.c | 29 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 29 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dlls/kernelbase/debug.c b/dlls/kernelbase/debug.c
index 6615507..e9da375 100644
--- a/dlls/kernelbase/debug.c
+++ b/dlls/kernelbase/debug.c
@@ -748,6 +748,29 @@ static BOOL check_resource_write( void *addr )
 }
 
 
+/*******************************************************************
+ *         ps5_no_debugger
+ *
+ * Whether this process is a PS5 title's or one of its helpers (the starter sets WINE_PS5_NTDLL_DIR for both): no
+ * debugger starts there. winedbg is not part of the runtime, and trying to start it reads AeDebug and allocates the
+ * command line and the environment from the process heap, which the crashing thread's neighbours may hold: the
+ * crash then froze the title instead of ending it.
+ */
+static BOOL ps5_no_debugger(void)
+{
+    static LONG state;   /* 0: not asked, 1: a title, 2: not */
+    WCHAR value[2];
+    SIZE_T len;
+
+    if (!state)
+    {
+        NTSTATUS status = RtlQueryEnvironmentVariable( NULL, L"WINE_PS5_NTDLL_DIR", 18, value, ARRAY_SIZE(value) - 1, &len );
+        InterlockedExchange( &state, status == STATUS_VARIABLE_NOT_FOUND ? 2 : 1 );
+    }
+    return state == 1;
+}
+
+
 /*******************************************************************
  *         UnhandledExceptionFilter   (kernelbase.@)
  */
@@ -784,6 +807,12 @@ LONG WINAPI UnhandledExceptionFilter( EXCEPTION_POINTERS *epointers )
             if (ret != EXCEPTION_CONTINUE_SEARCH) return ret;
         }
 
+        if (ps5_no_debugger())
+        {
+            ERR( "unhandled exception %#lx at %p: no debugger starts in a PS5 title\n", rec->ExceptionCode, rec->ExceptionAddress );
+            return nested ? EXCEPTION_CONTINUE_SEARCH : EXCEPTION_EXECUTE_HANDLER;
+        }
+
         if ((GetErrorMode() & SEM_NOGPFAULTERRORBOX) ||
             !start_debugger_atomic( epointers ) || !NtCurrentTeb()->Peb->BeingDebugged)
             return nested ? EXCEPTION_CONTINUE_SEARCH : EXCEPTION_EXECUTE_HANDLER;
